    {
      "id": "t_32",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1480,
      "width": 1381.1190185546875,
      "height": 140,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#495057",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b00",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2046634025,
      "version": 2,
      "versionNonce": 724877255,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1794691500960,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "• tRPC mutations enqueue work with inngest.send(\"agent/run\" | \"github/export\"); Inngest then calls back into /api/inngest to run each durable step.\n• Every server box reads and writes Postgres through Prisma; only the main arrows are drawn.\n• export-github pushes with the user's OAuth token on the server; no credential ever enters a sandbox or the model context.\n• Supermemory receives only the user's own message text (read in route, written in remember); Browserbase only the preview URL and rendered pages.\n• Notification emails: run-agent and export-github queue notify/send; send-notification emails the user through Resend (project name and outcome only, never prompts or code).\n• Editing: code.write saves a draft version and updates the running sandbox; Save version, or the next message, makes it a saved version.\n  /api/terminal runs one command at a time. Editing and the terminal both lock while an agent runs.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "• tRPC mutations enqueue work with inngest.send(\"agent/run\" | \"github/export\"); Inngest then calls back into /api/inngest to run each durable step.\n• Every server box reads and writes Postgres through Prisma; only the main arrows are drawn.\n• export-github pushes with the user's OAuth token on the server; no credential ever enters a sandbox or the model context.\n• Supermemory receives only the user's own message text (read in route, written in remember); Browserbase only the preview URL and rendered pages.\n• Notification emails: run-agent and export-github queue notify/send; send-notification emails the user through Resend (project name and outcome only, never prompts or code).\n• Editing: code.write saves a draft version and updates the running sandbox; Save version, or the next message, makes it a saved version.\n  /api/terminal runs one command at a time. Editing and the terminal both lock while an agent runs.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
